1
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:14,257
So that's where you were hiding, boss.

2
00:00:14,340 --> 00:00:15,197
Found you.

3
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:16,417
Thank God.

4
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:18,618
Guess that's gonna be your new body.

5
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:23,377
I can remember when my soul
slipped away before I conked out.

6
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:28,900
You told me that you had to go, that
you would make it right, I believe.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,460
As long as you're in the game, that you'll
bring it all home for the both of us.

8
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:43,300
But still, I miss you.

9
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,420
It would mean the world
if you'd call again,

10
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:52,960
boss.

11
00:01:19,020 --> 00:01:20,844
Thank you so much for watching.

12
00:01:36,540 --> 00:01:40,380
The truth is the end of
the day, or the future

13
00:01:54,780 --> 00:01:55,920
RECRIAMO!

14
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:04,860
Nessuno può succedere un destino scelto.

15
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:10,080
Roman solo il risultato
che voi sarete distrutti.

16
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:15,300
L 'eterna cima esiste solo per me.

17
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:20,920
Puoi cantare canzoni di
tristezza nel Monday senza tempo.

18
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:29,720
The fear of regretting the world,
the challenge of the world is now.

19
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:32,200
Let's go to peace of mind.

20
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:35,169
When it takes a nap,
this feeling will PDF,

21
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:39,620
the joy of the beginning.

22
00:02:53,780 --> 00:02:54,610
Huh?

23
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:55,790
Vista!

24
00:02:55,873 --> 00:02:56,777
The time has come!

25
00:02:56,860 --> 00:02:59,036
Take the arrow and impale your stand!

26
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:00,050
What the hell?

27
00:03:00,133 --> 00:03:00,963
He did a 180!

28
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:03,380
He's coming in real hot! Druno!

29
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:05,337
You have to try and stop him now!

30
00:03:05,420 --> 00:03:06,250
It's too far!

31
00:03:06,333 --> 00:03:07,163
I can't!

32
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:12,032
You've gotta be kidding!

33
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:13,671
What are you waiting for?

34
00:03:13,820 --> 00:03:15,237
It's cause you've got the arrow!

35
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:16,160
Just my luck!

36
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:19,040
It had to crap out now!
The arrow! Quickly!

37
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:20,680
Let go of it!

38
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:30,932
It's a good thing I thought to swipe
that stupid Kotz Beretta just in case.

39
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:32,788
But what the hell, bullets?

40
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:36,096
None of you told me my
revolver was in such bad shape.

41
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:39,220
What if it was the boss who broke it?

42
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:41,140
You idiot.

43
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:43,857
Feet before opening that
big mouth, number five.

44
00:03:43,940 --> 00:03:44,897
Look around, moron.

45
00:03:44,980 --> 00:03:46,237
There ain't nothing here but air.

46
00:03:46,320 --> 00:03:48,117
So how could the boss even touch us?

47
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:49,030
Huh?

48
00:03:49,113 --> 00:03:52,137
I didn't see anyone near us
when the darn thing broke.

49
00:03:52,220 --> 00:03:53,440
It's metal fatigue.

50
00:03:53,740 --> 00:03:54,997
You've been using it too much.

51
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:56,256
It's totally normal.

52
00:03:56,480 --> 00:03:58,520
Look, the damn crane's giving out.

53
00:03:58,740 --> 00:04:02,211
All this fighting with no
maintenance can't be good for it.

54
00:04:02,540 --> 00:04:03,370
Hey!

55
00:04:12,660 --> 00:04:14,180
Give me a break!

56
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:17,177
How many more times am I
gonna have to shoot your ass?

57
00:04:17,260 --> 00:04:19,397
Wait, it's my life he's after now.

58
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:22,440
Simply having the arrow
back is no longer enough.

59
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:24,260
Golden wind!

60
00:04:29,860 --> 00:04:31,000
Yes, of course.

61
00:04:31,220 --> 00:04:35,017
Requiem now seeks to punish me
because I dared to touch the arrow.

62
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:35,930
Mister, run!

63
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:38,460
A little help, guys?

64
00:04:38,780 --> 00:04:39,860
Where's my reload?

65
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:41,660
That isn't a revolver!

66
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:43,517
We're gonna need a new magazine!

67
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:45,659
It might take us longer than usual!

68
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:49,020
It's no use.

69
00:04:53,500 --> 00:04:54,330
I'm...

70
00:04:57,420 --> 00:04:58,250
Joino!

71
00:04:58,420 --> 00:04:59,655
Got something for ya!

72
00:05:00,220 --> 00:05:02,080
I'm gonna throw it! Go wide!

73
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:09,270
Goddammit!

74
00:05:23,540 --> 00:05:25,100
Hey, Mr. Polnareff!

75
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:28,897
He looks fine, but still, how did...

76
00:05:28,980 --> 00:05:33,520
Mista, take a moment to think back on
what I said to you at the Colosseum.

77
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:38,760
I confess to not fully grasping
the extent of Requiem's powers.

78
00:05:39,620 --> 00:05:41,220
That has now changed.

79
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:44,794
With his true plans in motion,
he's lost interest in me.

80
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:46,897
What do you mean, his true plans?

81
00:05:46,980 --> 00:05:50,340
They're unfurling before your very eyes!

82
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:52,420
I'm beginning to mutate!

83
00:05:52,580 --> 00:05:54,992
That's why Requiem gave up on chasing me!

84
00:05:56,720 --> 00:05:59,640
This is but the first
stage in his grand plan!

85
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:03,040
His intentions weren't
merely to swap our souls.

86
00:06:03,320 --> 00:06:07,380
He seeded our transformation
into completely new beings!

87
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:09,760
The prelude is over.

88
00:06:09,900 --> 00:06:11,420
Now comes the crescendo!

89
00:06:11,860 --> 00:06:13,978
Whether or not I live is irrelevant!

90
00:06:14,780 --> 00:06:17,677
The history of the world
has unfolded on its

91
00:06:17,760 --> 00:06:20,289
own path for four and
a half billion years.

92
00:06:20,780 --> 00:06:24,133
Requiem will thrust it on a
new one in a matter of hours.

93
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:25,750
Fascinating.

94
00:06:25,840 --> 00:06:28,722
The true nature of his
powers has been laid bare.

95
00:06:30,020 --> 00:06:31,220
Crazy, children.

96
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:34,240
Your help has been most invaluable to me.

97
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:37,440
The path forward is finally clear.

98
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:39,780
With nothing left in my way,

99
00:06:39,960 --> 00:06:43,440
the arrow will soon be mine,
and it's all thanks to you!

100
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:47,089
What the hell is
happening to these people?

101
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:48,780
His power's insane!

102
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:51,615
You said this is happening everywhere?

103
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:55,497
It doesn't look like it's causing
them any sort of pain, at least.

104
00:06:55,580 --> 00:06:58,168
They've all got blank
stares in their faces.

105
00:06:58,280 --> 00:07:02,940
But even so, I can't shake the horrible
thought that my body's gonna mutate.

106
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:04,989
This can't be real, right?

107
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:09,633
Am I seriously gonna mold piece by
piece until there's nothing left of me?

108
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:11,130
Trish!

109
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:13,220
I'm fine, I think.

110
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:16,158
There's no stopping the process now.

111
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:20,740
In a few short hours, we will all
have finished our damnable mutations.

112
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:23,237
Then we better not waste even a second.

113
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:24,496
Let's get a move on.

114
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:25,720
You did this!

115
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:27,977
You just had to touch
the arrow, didn't ya?

116
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:30,657
Defeat Diavolo, my big
fat hairy stinking ass!

117
00:07:30,740 --> 00:07:32,817
All the arrow has done
is end our life sooner!

118
00:07:32,900 --> 00:07:33,730
That's enough!

119
00:07:33,813 --> 00:07:35,737
There's no way in hell he
could have foreseen this!

120
00:07:35,820 --> 00:07:39,114
We must refocus and figure
out how to take down Requiem!

121
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:45,170
That's right.

122
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:46,620
Run to him, you fools.

123
00:07:46,900 --> 00:07:48,253
Move in nice and close.

124
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:51,977
I can feel the remainder
of his secrets unraveling

125
00:07:52,060 --> 00:07:54,531
faster and faster with each step you take.

126
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:59,176
Let me seize the power of the arrow
so the world may grovel at my feet.

127
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:00,735
We've almost got him!

128
00:08:00,840 --> 00:08:01,670
Good.

129
00:08:01,753 --> 00:08:03,401
Everybody stand still, right now!

130
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:04,710
That's it!

131
00:08:04,793 --> 00:08:05,623
Stay far apart!

132
00:08:05,706 --> 00:08:07,440
And don't move a muscle! What?

133
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,647
I told you to freeze, Mista!

134
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:12,391
We'll have to catch up with Requiem later!

135
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:13,814
What the hell, Giorno?

136
00:08:13,900 --> 00:08:15,097
You trying to get us killed?

137
00:08:15,180 --> 00:08:17,677
In case you haven't
noticed, my body's melting!

138
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:19,937
I took a closer look at your revolver.

139
00:08:20,020 --> 00:08:21,667
The one you said just broke?

140
00:08:21,840 --> 00:08:23,257
Something's off about it.

141
00:08:23,340 --> 00:08:25,737
The broken piece doesn't fit quite right.

142
00:08:25,820 --> 00:08:27,357
That shouldn't be the case.

143
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:31,240
If it really were Metal Fatigue,
the pieces would fit perfectly.

144
00:08:31,700 --> 00:08:34,280
Giorno, what exactly are you saying?

145
00:08:34,540 --> 00:08:36,481
I need you to stay in place, too!

146
00:08:36,740 --> 00:08:38,757
Trust me, I know what I'm talking about!

147
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:39,700
Hey, asshole!

148
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:40,917
Requiem's getting away!

149
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:44,897
If the bullets say it's because the stupid
gun gave out, then that's what freakin'

150
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:45,810
happened!

151
00:08:45,893 --> 00:08:46,723
End of story!

152
00:08:46,806 --> 00:08:48,417
Besides, it got me the sweeperetta now!

153
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:52,265
The two pieces don't fit right,
cause a chunk probably fell off!

154
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:53,581
That's possible.

155
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:57,057
But it's far more likely
to be something else.

156
00:08:57,140 --> 00:09:00,560
We'll know for sure as soon
as we get that lost piece.

157
00:09:02,060 --> 00:09:03,617
Let's take a look, Golden Wind.

158
00:09:03,700 --> 00:09:06,437
I gave part of the gun
life and let it run loose.

159
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:09,049
It's blind, but its
nose makes up for that.

160
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:11,691
It can pick up things our eyes might miss.

161
00:09:12,180 --> 00:09:13,709
Little guy just proved it.

162
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:16,489
He's found a critical
piece of this puzzle.

163
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:23,960
Dude, come on. Forget them all.

164
00:09:24,140 --> 00:09:27,957
I already told you it's impossible
for another person to have done this.

165
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:29,000
So drop it.

166
00:09:29,140 --> 00:09:30,297
Bullets and I aren't stupid.

167
00:09:30,380 --> 00:09:32,077
We know what we're talking about.

168
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:35,157
Nobody got anywhere close to me
when the damn revolver broke.

169
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:36,070
But that's it.

170
00:09:36,153 --> 00:09:36,983
There's no one here.

171
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:38,677
That's why we're standing apart.

172
00:09:38,760 --> 00:09:41,172
Remember, his range is just a few meters.

173
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:44,180
Giorno, are you?

174
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:48,465
No one got anywhere close to
Narancia when he was killed either.

175
00:09:49,080 --> 00:09:51,220
No one besides any of us.

176
00:09:52,780 --> 00:09:53,610
Mr.

177
00:09:53,693 --> 00:09:55,720
Polnareff, if it really is as you say,

178
00:09:55,900 --> 00:09:58,877
and the boss does turn out
to possess two personas,

179
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:02,195
that means his soul could
reside in anybody he chooses.

180
00:10:03,020 --> 00:10:06,460
My guess, Diavolo is hiding
out inside one of us. What?

181
00:10:08,300 --> 00:10:09,480
Just think about it.

182
00:10:09,680 --> 00:10:12,357
Why hasn't Trish been able
to sense him this whole time?

183
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:13,957
And that's not the only thing.

184
00:10:14,040 --> 00:10:17,037
He's also waiting for us to
die doing his dirty work.

185
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:18,179
Do you get it now?

186
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:20,679
He's the reason why your gun broke.

187
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:25,750
Come on!

188
00:10:25,833 --> 00:10:26,797
Stay right where you are, Mista!

189
00:10:26,880 --> 00:10:27,998
I'll tell it again!

190
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:30,217
We have to remain out of his range!

191
00:10:30,300 --> 00:10:32,397
I'm the one whose gun
was destroyed, moron!

192
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:36,700
And the person closest to it was you, too.

193
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:39,520
There's no way it's me!

194
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:41,060
Wait, hold on.

195
00:10:41,340 --> 00:10:44,040
Right before Narancia
got killed, let's see.

196
00:10:44,260 --> 00:10:46,460
The closest one was...

197
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:53,840
Merda, I have to act quickly.

198
00:10:54,620 --> 00:10:57,200
Requiem is about to slip from my grasp.

199
00:10:57,800 --> 00:11:00,717
Churno Chuvana, you pestilent brat!

200
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:02,640
He's inside one of us.

201
00:11:02,780 --> 00:11:04,368
That's all I know for sure.

202
00:11:04,780 --> 00:11:08,545
What might not be obvious is we've
got him backed into a corner.

203
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:12,237
Diavolo might be able to
sic Emperor Crimson on us,

204
00:11:12,320 --> 00:11:15,614
but he still can't completely
control his physical host.

205
00:11:16,740 --> 00:11:21,117
If he did have that kind of freedom, there'd
be no need for him to use subterfuge.

206
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:22,920
He'd just finish us all off.

207
00:11:23,740 --> 00:11:28,564
It's exactly because he's so constrained
that we're all still standing here alive.

208
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:30,620
We have the upper hand.

209
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:32,487
Let's not waste this chance.

210
00:11:33,540 --> 00:11:34,960
What if it's the turtle?

211
00:11:35,280 --> 00:11:37,957
He was the only one around
me when my revolver broke.

212
00:11:38,040 --> 00:11:40,477
So it's got to be Polnareff
who got possessed.

213
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:41,577
That can't be the case.

214
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:45,017
In case you've forgotten, Requiem
almost killed him just now.

215
00:11:45,100 --> 00:11:47,688
And only because the
boss broke your weapon.

216
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:51,826
The boss wouldn't risk letting
injury befall his physical host.

217
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:56,780
Besides, I can only
sense one soul in there.

218
00:11:57,700 --> 00:12:00,197
He's a singular turtle
with only one spirit.

219
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:02,580
You can discern souls? That's good.

220
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:04,021
There's a catch.

221
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:08,040
If I can't make direct
physical contact, then no.

222
00:12:08,300 --> 00:12:09,712
How does that even work?

223
00:12:10,060 --> 00:12:11,900
Life energy comes in clusters.

224
00:12:12,620 --> 00:12:15,444
Direct touch tells me how
many souls in a clump.

225
00:12:15,920 --> 00:12:17,040
No other way.

226
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:20,325
I'll have to touch each
of you briefly to know.

227
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:22,482
There still remains one problem.

228
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:25,092
What if you fall within the boss's range?

229
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:30,740
I've got a trick for that. Mr.

230
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:32,977
Polnareff kindly taught it to me earlier.

231
00:12:33,060 --> 00:12:36,197
I just have to look for a
sudden increase in blood drops.

232
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:38,221
That'll tell me if time has left.

233
00:12:39,980 --> 00:12:43,745
That might help you detect him,
but the rest will all be on you.

234
00:12:43,980 --> 00:12:45,320
The fates be willing.

235
00:12:45,700 --> 00:12:48,759
You might just be able to
narrowly dodge his strike.

236
00:12:53,780 --> 00:12:55,580
Look, it's definitely not me.

237
00:12:56,140 --> 00:12:57,397
I mean, there's no way.

238
00:12:57,480 --> 00:12:59,833
I was the furthest person from Narancia.

239
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:04,400
Then why don't I just examine you
first and get it over with? What?

240
00:13:04,900 --> 00:13:06,460
You can stop right there.

241
00:13:06,720 --> 00:13:08,014
Don't come any closer!

242
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:10,540
Stay back!

243
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:15,676
What if Diavolo's hiding in you, huh?

244
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:17,220
Then what happens?

245
00:13:18,020 --> 00:13:21,780
By the time Narancia died,
his body was an empty shell.

246
00:13:23,780 --> 00:13:28,192
I know because my soul could travel
seamlessly into it, nothing stopped me.

247
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:32,492
That's why I'm sure it's just me in here.

248
00:13:35,260 --> 00:13:37,860
Well, gee, that's a
super reassuring story,

249
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:41,473
is what I'd say if I had any
way of confirming it's true.

250
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:42,980
I mean, come on!

251
00:13:43,220 --> 00:13:47,197
How could you know for sure the boss
isn't actually hiding somewhere in there?

252
00:13:47,280 --> 00:13:50,917
It doesn't look like you can check
yourself with that ability, can you?

253
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:54,412
Mista, if you keep this up,
we can kiss the arrow goodbye!

254
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:57,011
Stop or you'll kiss your kneecaps goodbye!

255
00:14:01,940 --> 00:14:02,920
Stop it now!

256
00:14:05,860 --> 00:14:08,280
You can check me first, Giorno.

257
00:14:10,260 --> 00:14:11,780
Come on, just do it!

258
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:14,353
We've wasted too much time on bickering.

259
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:15,892
It's just like you said.

260
00:14:16,320 --> 00:14:19,397
We should seize the chance to hit
the boss while he's vulnerable.

261
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:22,340
There's no other way. Let's go.

262
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:24,560
We must proceed quickly.

263
00:14:34,300 --> 00:14:36,180
Someone's dying. I know it.

264
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:38,480
If we move closer...

265
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:58,220
It was Mista!

266
00:14:58,520 --> 00:15:00,137
The boss was hiding inside him!

267
00:15:00,220 --> 00:15:01,980
Spicy lady! Trish, no!

268
00:15:02,300 --> 00:15:03,300
He was in you!

269
00:15:04,020 --> 00:15:08,740
At horrifying speed, he was able to close
the distance in nearly no time at all!

270
00:15:09,840 --> 00:15:13,340
Sweet daughter, I've been
waiting for this moment.

271
00:15:13,780 --> 00:15:16,800
Your stand finally appears before me!

272
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:29,160
My Trish, had you not foolishly
revealed your stand to me,

273
00:15:29,400 --> 00:15:33,180
your dear friends may very well
have succeeded in their gambit.

274
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:34,540
Release her at once!

275
00:15:39,020 --> 00:15:41,820
As long as your stand is in my grasp,

276
00:15:42,100 --> 00:15:46,540
I fear you're little more than a
puppet enslaved to my every whim.

277
00:15:46,940 --> 00:15:48,117
He's going for a strike.

278
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:49,397
Brace yourselves, quick!

279
00:15:49,480 --> 00:15:50,617
Time is about to...

280
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:51,580
Huh?

281
00:15:54,260 --> 00:15:55,090
Where is he?

282
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:57,937
Did he forget to murder us first?

283
00:15:58,020 --> 00:15:59,373
Why is he running away?

284
00:15:59,480 --> 00:16:02,517
It's likely we're not at the
top of his list right now.

285
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:05,129
His focus seems to be
on seizing the arrow.

286
00:16:05,420 --> 00:16:08,557
It's the only real thing that
matters, and he knows it.

287
00:16:08,640 --> 00:16:09,557
Shoot him, Mista.

288
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:11,875
He can't be allowed to reach it first.

289
00:16:14,580 --> 00:16:15,940
Pull the damn trigger!

290
00:16:16,220 --> 00:16:19,749
A few bullet wounds are nothing
compared to what he will do.

291
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:23,877
I know the problem is
I've already shot him.

292
00:16:23,960 --> 00:16:26,760
I counted fired all six shots

293
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:40,057
That bastards messing
with time as he's running

294
00:16:40,140 --> 00:16:42,964
if he sees him coming my
bullets can't touch him

295
00:16:44,020 --> 00:16:46,800
After him it's all over
if he gets that arrow

296
00:16:54,020 --> 00:16:59,897
that shadow it must hold the key to the
arrows imperviousness let's see if my

297
00:16:59,980 --> 00:17:05,297
theory proves to be correct requiem's
shadow always extends in the direction

298
00:17:05,380 --> 00:17:11,977
opposing my movements regardless of the
sun's actual position that must mean

299
00:17:12,060 --> 00:17:16,880
to that man's eyes the shadow should
appear as if it is stretching toward me.

300
00:17:17,220 --> 00:17:21,780
But to Bucciarati, the shadow is
extending in front of Requiem itself.

301
00:17:22,140 --> 00:17:22,970
In other

302
00:17:23,680 --> 00:17:27,837
words, the position of the shadow
depends on the position of the observer.

303
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:30,940
Cretanous shade, your
powers are no mystery.

304
00:17:31,260 --> 00:17:33,900
I understand how you manipulate souls.

305
00:17:34,260 --> 00:17:36,495
Requiem is the silhouette of the soul.

306
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:40,251
To face it is to contend with
the shadow of one's own mind.

307
00:17:40,540 --> 00:17:44,737
Therefore, attacking Making it is futile,
it's akin to attacking one's self.

308
00:17:44,820 --> 00:17:48,060
If I eliminate this shadow,
the arrow will be mine.

309
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:53,460
Well then, wherever a shadow treads,
a source of light must also be nearby.

310
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:56,141
He still hasn't gotten the arrow.

311
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:57,280
Go for Brokmista!

312
00:17:58,080 --> 00:18:01,020
The only place it could
be is behind my soul!

313
00:18:06,040 --> 00:18:09,457
He struck something behind his
head, yet Requiem suffered the blow.

314
00:18:09,540 --> 00:18:10,893
What the hell happened?

315
00:18:12,300 --> 00:18:13,860
You're mine at last.

316
00:18:14,780 --> 00:18:18,700
Behold, the final victor
is I! I don't care.

317
00:18:19,020 --> 00:18:23,477
Even if Diavolo somehow gets his vile
hands on the arrow, the fight goes on.

318
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:24,795
We'll just improvise.

319
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:29,844
Lucky for me, the blood he spilled when
he severed my arm is just ordinary matter.

320
00:18:30,020 --> 00:18:31,902
No different from anything else.

321
00:18:33,240 --> 00:18:35,480
Now ain't that right, Golden Wind?

322
00:18:37,580 --> 00:18:38,700
It's showtime!

323
00:18:39,380 --> 00:18:40,357
What's happening?

324
00:18:40,440 --> 00:18:42,200
Bring that damn mongrel!

325
00:18:44,520 --> 00:18:45,600
Not too bad.

326
00:18:46,300 --> 00:18:49,040
I gotta catch up with them quick!

327
00:18:51,560 --> 00:18:52,840
Fire again, Mista!

328
00:18:52,980 --> 00:18:54,197
Don't let him get too close!

329
00:18:54,280 --> 00:18:55,320
Yeah, I know!

330
00:18:58,320 --> 00:18:59,150
Gotcha!

331
00:18:59,233 --> 00:19:01,537
Bet you didn't predict
that, you freakin' idiot!

332
00:19:01,620 --> 00:19:03,577
Deflect the bullets coming
at you all you want,

333
00:19:03,660 --> 00:19:06,197
you can't do jack shit
about these other guys!

334
00:19:06,280 --> 00:19:09,515
All right, fellas, y 'all
flick that baby back to Papa!

335
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:11,270
Gah!

336
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:18,300
He just launched a whole person!

337
00:19:18,520 --> 00:19:20,057
All the way toward the arrow!

338
00:19:20,140 --> 00:19:22,081
So he did predict our trajectory!

339
00:19:22,240 --> 00:19:24,057
He used the body to course correct!

340
00:19:24,140 --> 00:19:26,720
Did you truly believe, even for a moment,

341
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:32,320
that your laughably slow wits could ever
hope to overcome my predictive mastery?

342
00:19:32,740 --> 00:19:37,120
There are no flaws to exploit, as
I'm sure you've recently learned.

343
00:19:37,460 --> 00:19:38,880
However, Bucciarati,

344
00:19:39,540 --> 00:19:42,380
You and your gaggle did
manage to make me try.

345
00:19:43,560 --> 00:19:47,800
I never imagined you would be foolish
enough to betray your own familia.

346
00:19:48,320 --> 00:19:52,360
Nor did I believe you competent
enough to discover my true identity.

347
00:19:52,840 --> 00:19:57,100
But I'm grateful this path has led
me to the true power of the arrow.

348
00:19:57,460 --> 00:19:58,580
Fate never fails.

349
00:19:58,860 --> 00:20:03,037
A fitting reward for ones who have
conquered the adversity of their past.

350
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:04,944
Guys, Reload, don't just stare.

351
00:20:05,060 --> 00:20:06,377
We already told you.

352
00:20:06,460 --> 00:20:09,578
That magazine takes us a
little bit longer to refill!

353
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:11,950
Shit!

354
00:20:12,120 --> 00:20:13,296
We're all gonna die!

355
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:20,630
No.

356
00:20:20,860 --> 00:20:21,720
What now?

357
00:20:22,380 --> 00:20:24,280
Spicy lady.

358
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:26,310
Surprise!

359
00:20:26,620 --> 00:20:28,077
You didn't deflect squat.

360
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:29,336
The bullets bounced.

361
00:20:29,420 --> 00:20:30,380
My secret?

362
00:20:30,620 --> 00:20:32,317
I turned them to chewing gum.

363
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:37,282
They stretched out thin as they flew, But
they clung to your fists the entire time.

364
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:40,820
Then they sprung back
to me and through you.

365
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:44,100
Trish, how long will you awake?

366
00:20:44,380 --> 00:20:46,720
I too will conquer my past.

367
00:20:46,980 --> 00:20:50,340
I refuse to be afraid, to
live in fear of my fate.

368
00:20:50,560 --> 00:20:52,180
I won't run from it.

369
00:20:52,600 --> 00:20:55,440
If it gets in my way, then I'll climb.

370
00:20:55,700 --> 00:20:57,053
It's as simple as that.

371
00:20:57,860 --> 00:20:59,340
The arrow! You guys!

372
00:20:59,620 --> 00:21:01,040
It's so damn close!

373
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:03,497
Holy crap, I almost got it!

374
00:21:03,580 --> 00:21:05,260
Kiss my ass, Diablo!

375
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:07,837
Go ahead and warp time or predict stuff!

376
00:21:07,920 --> 00:21:09,177
It won't change a thing!

377
00:21:09,260 --> 00:21:11,084
The arrow's coming to me, baby!

378
00:21:11,800 --> 00:21:17,300
My dear Geralt, how I wish I had never
brought you into this wretched world!

379
00:21:17,660 --> 00:21:20,100
Seems I've yet to break free of my past!

380
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:22,360
Curse it, worm!

381
00:21:23,420 --> 00:21:25,080
Now, I'm angry!

382
00:21:31,200 --> 00:21:32,740
No, it can't!

383
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:41,297
what was it you said
about fate you just climb

384
00:21:41,380 --> 00:21:45,140
am i right well i hope
you like flying instead

385
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:47,880
there you go

386
00:21:51,420 --> 00:21:52,820
Trash!

387
00:22:18,640 --> 00:22:23,177
Join us Come on I'll save us

388
00:22:23,260 --> 00:22:27,257
alive We are the power Who'll

389
00:22:27,340 --> 00:22:34,300
feed the future Cause we are
Fight us Just fighting for a ride

390
00:23:47,880 --> 00:23:51,160
Thank you.
